@baseUrl = http://localhost:5075
@clientId = SYNTH-001
@importId = {{importedWorkbooks.response.body.$[0].id}}

### Angular workflow: open http://localhost:4200/
### Upload only queues raw SQL import. It does not request prediction.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/clients/{{clientId}}/workbooks
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WorkbookBoundary

--WorkbookBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="SYNTH-001-FY2026.xlsx"
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet

< ../outputs/synthetic-workbooks/SYNTH-001-FY2026.xlsx
--WorkbookBoundary--

### Run this named request first after each startup to resolve the new import ID.
# @name importedWorkbooks
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/clients/{{clientId}}/workbooks

### Waiting files or rejection details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/clients/{{clientId}}/workbooks/inbox

### Explicit Categorize button action (change DPL to TFA or CRD)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/clients/{{clientId}}/workbooks/{{importId}}/categorize?type=DPL

### Background categorization run progress
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/clients/{{clientId}}/workbooks/{{importId}}/runs

### Verify logical batches of 20, 20, 10 for each requested type
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/clients/{{clientId}}/workbooks/{{importId}}/batches

### Read 20 saved SQL rows and their predictions (use skip=20 then skip=40)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/clients/{{clientId}}/workbooks/{{importId}}/records?type=DPL&skip=0&take=20

### Legacy single-description demo: get the synthetic example entries
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/categorization/examples

### Run the local ONNX model and retrieve similar examples
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/categorization/suggestions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "New laptops for the finance team",
  "count": 3
}
